    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "SF8Qg",
      "x": 4240,
      "y": 1272,
      "name": "Canvas feed — order & anchoring",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Canvas feed — order & anchoring\n\nEach AI answer that produces gen-UI renders as one canvas in the mainPanel feed. A canvas is an open section: it never draws its own surface, border, or shadow.\n\nOrder mirrors the chat: oldest at top, newest at the bottom. When an answer starts, the feed scrolls so the new canvas header sits spacing-md below the mainPanel top, then streams in. Canvas / Skeleton holds the space until the first block lands; Save stays disabled while streaming.\n\nBetween canvases: Canvas / Feed Divider (1px $g:sem-navDivider, gap 56). When the date changes, use Feed Divider / Day.\n\nIf the user has scrolled up when a new canvas arrives, don’t auto-scroll. Show Feed / New Canvas Pill instead.\n\nView area: max 1024 with min 40px gutters (chat-nav-refresh rule). With nav and chat open at 1440 the canvas is 744 wide; templates collapse at their breakpoints.\n\nNav and chat are pinned to the viewport (1024 tall here). Only the mainPanel scrolls; this frame is extended to show the whole feed."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "Rl52Q",
      "x": 4620,
      "y": 1272,
      "name": "Saving — states & toast",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Saving — states & toast\n\nSave lives in every canvas header (Canvas / Save Button, 7 states). Each state is a Hemlock Button/sm/outline/icon-left instance, so it's a pill like every other button.\n\nDefault → Pressed → Saving (Hemlock loading state; ignores clicks) → Saved. Saved keeps the Pressed style at rest. Hovering Saved shows Remove (bookmark-minus). Disabled while the canvas streams or when offline.\n\nOn success, show Canvas / Toast / Saved bottom-center of the view area, 24px above the viewport edge, for 5 seconds, with View saved and Undo. Removing shows Toast / Removed with Undo.\n\nOn failure, return the button to Default and show the toast with Retry in place of View saved: “Couldn’t save. Retry”.\n\nThe chat Canvas Link for the same canvas mirrors the state: its kicker becomes TYPE · SAVED with the bookmark-check icon.\n\nARIA: Save is a toggle button. aria-pressed is true when saved; the label switches between “Save canvas” and “Remove from saved”. The toast is a polite live region."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "HMm6F",
      "x": 5000,
      "y": 1272,
      "name": "Saved canvases — snapshot vs live",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Saved canvases — snapshot vs live\n\nSaving stores a snapshot: the rendered block JSON, the data values at save time, and the original question.\n\nOpening a saved canvas shows that snapshot under Canvas / Snapshot Bar / Snapshot. Refresh reruns the original question with today’s data in place and swaps the bar to Live. The saved copy stays unchanged until the user picks Update saved copy.\n\nSaved view: the page title lives in the page container (no header bar). Filter with Hemlock SegmentedControl (All · Reports · Plans · Explainers); sort with a text button. Grid is 2 columns of Saved / Tile, gap 48 across and 32 down; 1 column under 720.\n\nTile actions show on hover and focus: pin to Dashboard, share, remove. A pinned tile becomes a Dashboard widget (design-system §11)."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "Q4nRq",
      "x": 5380,
      "y": 1272,
      "name": "Chat ↔ canvas",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Chat ↔ canvas\n\nEvery AI turn that renders a canvas also posts a Chat / Canvas Link under the AI text. Clicking it scrolls the feed to that canvas and moves focus to the canvas title.\n\nExactly one link is In View at a time: the canvas whose header is nearest the top of the view area.\n\nPrompt chips appear under the latest AI reply only. Sending a message clears them from earlier turns.\n\nChat atoms (messages, chips, input, close FAB) belong to chat-nav-refresh.pen. They are copied here to show the views in place. Don’t edit them here."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "lP1HG",
      "x": 4240,
      "y": 2178,
      "name": "Nav — Canvases section (proposal)",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Nav — Canvases section (proposal)\n\nProposed for chat-nav-refresh: a CANVASES section above YOUR MONEY with Feed and Saved. Saved shows a count (font-ui, text-size-xs, $g:sem-navTextSecondary).\n\nThe active item uses $g:sem-navActiveBg with $g:sem-navTextPrimary at 600. chat-nav-refresh’s current active item binds $g:sem-borders-dark; sem-navActiveBg is the matching role.\n\nNeeds sign-off before it moves into chat-nav-refresh.pen."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "nM8Nd",
      "x": 4620,
      "y": 2178,
      "name": "Tokens & type in this file",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Tokens & type in this file\n\nDark is the default theme. The Light feed copy exists only to check that every color flips through tokens.\n\nColor, spacing, radius, and type-size bindings come from Hemlock (g: alias), with exceptions: some components still hardcode spacing values, and a few borrow nav or chat tokens. 02 Component Tokens (in the library) lists each one under Off Hemlock. The only local tokens are font-ui and nav-themeToggleIcon.\n\nfont-ui = Gothic A1 is an exploration stand-in for $g:font-primary (Heebo). To ship with Heebo, point font-ui at $g:font-primary; nothing else changes. Hemlock components inside canvases carry a fontFamily override to font-ui for the same reason.\n\nMeta text binds $g:sem-text-meta. In dark it measures 3.8:1 on sem-background-elevated and 4.3:1 on sem-background-main, under AA for small text. The fix is in progress in Hemlock; every meta role here is bound to the token, so the new value flows through."
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "id": "rwo6t",
      "x": -691,
      "y": 1739.549955842878,
      "opacity": 0.5,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 219,
      "content": "The color roles (Node ID: w7Te6) should reference more than what it's referencing now, because, for instance, there will be more categorical chart colors than just the 5 shown here. And in fact, do we need it all if everything here should be referencing the hemlock library? Devs have that hemlock library. we really just need what each component is spec'd with (including text components). The tokens should not be straying at all from the hemlock system and if they are, tell me!"
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "id": "wPpvW",
      "x": 2457,
      "y": -322,
      "width": 397,
      "height": 250,
      "content": "Instead of \"canvases\", we will have \"artifacts\" and also \"plans\". We will need a \"plan\" component template to implement for various purposes, from retirement planning to savings goals to estate planning to tax strategy and beyond; and when a user saves a \"plan\", it get saved to Plans, not Artifacts. Other answers get saved to \"Artifacts\""
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "id": "X8JmK7",
      "x": 2891.2058036608605,
      "y": -261.57250440007147,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 219,
      "content": "We need to add \"Conversations\" to the left side nav, with the ability to intuitively rename, reorder, and delete conversations."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "LIJPO",
      "x": 3739,
      "y": -249,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 219,
      "content": "Create a status of a report being made in progress - potentially put this in the Chat header, where \"Chat\" used to appear."
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "id": "wONg0",
      "x": 4291.524771056278,
      "y": -262.7781584814112,
      "width": 402,
      "height": 250,
      "content": "Change \"Saved canvases\" to \"Library\" and then library will be comprised of Live Artifacts (e.g., dashboard, tables, explainers, etc.), Plans, Reports (e.g., Spreadsheets, Presentations, PDFs, etc.), and Meeting Notes. There may be more categories added later."
    },
