    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "DqYA0",
      "x": 4520,
      "y": 4323,
      "name": "Conversations nav — structure & order",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Conversations nav — structure & order\n\nCONVERSATIONS replaces the CANVASES section (Feed and Saved). Each conversation is its own feed: opening one loads its chat in the chat panel and its canvases in the mainPanel. Saved is dropped for now and comes back as Library.\n\nThe section sits below YOUR MONEY and takes the rest of the nav height. The list scrolls on its own; YOUR MONEY and the user area stay put, and the existing bottom fade shows there's more.\n\nOrder is manual. New conversations go on top. New activity never reshuffles the list, so a row stays where the user put it.\n\nTitles wrap to two lines, then truncate with an ellipsis; the full title shows in a tooltip.\n\nThe open conversation uses Active (sem-navActiveBg, 600) with aria-current=\"page\".\n\nOpen: where \"New conversation\" lives (for example a + on the CONVERSATIONS header) isn't designed yet."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "KpTBX",
      "x": 4900,
      "y": 4323,
      "name": "Conversations nav — moving rows",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Conversations nav — moving rows\n\nHover or focus a row: the drag handle appears in the left gutter (the section chevron's column) and the More button appears on the right. Over the handle the cursor is the system grab hand (CSS cursor: grab). Handle and More keep their space when hidden, so titles never reflow. There is no Reorder item in the More menu; the handle is the only cue.\n\nDrag is the interaction for everyone: press the handle (or anywhere on the row once the pointer moves 4px) and drag. A plain click on the row still opens the conversation.\n\nWhile carried, the cursor is the system closed hand (cursor: grabbing). The row lifts (Dragging: elevated fill, shadow-lg), stays on the list's vertical axis, and moves on top of the rows it passes, partly covering them. Its old slot stays open until it crosses the next row's middle; then that row slides into the slot. The list auto-scrolls near its top and bottom edges. Esc puts the row back.\n\nFallbacks, invisible to anyone who drags (no screen-reader detection needed; browsers don't expose it reliably anyway):\n• Click the handle without moving: the row lifts and follows the pointer; click again to drop. Covers pointer users who can't drag (WCAG 2.5.7) and never fires during a drag.\n• Screen readers: each row carries visually hidden Move up / Move down buttons. Keyboard: Tab to the handle, Space picks up, ↑ / ↓ move, Space or Enter drops, Esc cancels. A polite live region announces each step, e.g. \"Emergency fund target, position 1 of 18.\"\n\nMobile: see \"Conversations nav — mobile\".\n\nCursors in the views are the macOS system cursors, drawn as annotations (gen-ui-canvas-assets/)."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "i4T4Gx",
      "x": 5280,
      "y": 4323,
      "name": "Conversations nav — rename & remove",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Conversations nav — rename & remove\n\nRename: More › Rename, or double-click the title. The row becomes an inline field (Hemlock Input/focus recipe) with the whole title selected, so typing replaces it. Enter or clicking away saves; Esc cancels. An empty title reverts. Max 80 characters; the field scrolls sideways while editing.\n\nRemove: More › Remove takes the row out at once, with no dialog. The toast (Canvas / Toast / Removed with new copy: \"Conversation removed · Undo\") sits bottom-center of the view area for 5 seconds and pauses while hovered or focused. Undo puts the row back where it was. The delete becomes permanent when the toast closes.\n\nRemoving the open conversation starts a new, empty one. Saved canvases from a removed conversation stay in Saved; they are snapshots.\n\nThe More menu opens 4px below the row, right edges aligned, and flips above near the viewport bottom. It renders in a top layer so the nav's clip can't cut it off. Arrow keys move through items; Esc closes it and returns focus to More."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "T6zUb",
      "x": 5660,
      "y": 4323,
      "name": "Conversations nav — tokens & Hemlock gaps",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Conversations nav — tokens & Hemlock gaps\n\nEverything binds Hemlock tokens: nav roles for rows (sem-navHoverBg, sem-navActiveBg, sem-navTextPrimary, sem-navTextSecondary, sem-navHoverText), sem-dragHandle for the handle, and Hemlock's dropdown recipe for the menu (sem-background-elevated, sem-borders-dark, radius-2xs, shadow-md). The carried row uses sem-background-elevated, sem-borders-dark and shadow-lg. More is Hemlock Button/sm/text/icon-only, pressed while its menu is open. Cursors are the browser's system defaults (grab, grabbing, pointer), not custom images.\n\nWhere Hemlock falls short:\n• Dark: sem-navHoverBg and sem-navActiveBg are the same value (#18223A), so a hovered row next to the open one reads as one block. Only the 600 weight tells them apart. Light is fine.\n• Dark: sem-background-rowHover on sem-background-elevated is about 1.05:1, so menu hover and focus barely show. Hemlock's AccountSelector has the same pairing. Needs a menu-hover role.\n• Rows inherit the nav's literal 13px text from chat-nav-refresh (no Hemlock size between text-size-xs 12 and text-size-sm 14). Titles also pin a 16px line (1.2308). Without an explicit line height, Pencil currently lays 13px text on a 13px line, so unpinned nav rows render about 27 tall instead of 30, the existing views included."
    },
