      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "u68MHP",
          "name": "Section Head",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$g:spacing-2xs",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Q8NRH6",
              "name": "Num",
              "fill": "$g:sem-text-meta",
              "content": "PROPOSAL · CANVAS BLOCKS · PLAIN TEXT FOR TEXT-LED ANSWERS",
              "lineHeight": "$g:line-height-2xs",
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$g:text-size-2xs",
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "SMfu5",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$g:sem-text-header",
              "content": "Paragraphs and lists",
              "lineHeight": "$g:line-height-3xl",
              "fontFamily": "$g:font-secondary",
              "fontSize": "$g:text-size-3xl",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "r85ok6",
              "name": "Desc",
              "fill": "$g:sem-text-body",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1100,
              "content": "Blocks for answers that are mostly words. Paragraph wraps Type / Body at the 680 measure, with an optional H3. A list marker sits on the first line of its item, pinned to the item's top-left, and the text is inset, so wrapped lines align with the text instead of the marker. Markers are structure, not actions, so they never take the link blue: bullets are a small diamond, the logo's dot, in sem-icons-info-strong, the info accent; numbers use Canvas / Number Marker, the Ranked Row's soft disc, so every numbered thing on a canvas looks the same. An item with a lead stacks a 600 lead line over the body. Rhythm: blocks inside a section sit spacing-sm apart; list items spacing-2xs (spacing-sm when they have leads); a section (an H2 and its blocks) sits spacing-lg from the next. On narrow views every block fills the column. Every value is a Hemlock token; font-ui is this file's stand-in for font-primary.",
              "lineHeight": "$g:line-height-sm",
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": "$g:text-size-sm",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
